# requirements-dev.in — the type checker CI runs (what we DECLARE)
# ==================================================================
# `mypy --strict --explicit-package-bases tools/` is a blocking CI job. These
# stay pinned exactly: a new mypy or stub release can add strict errors, and
# that upgrade should be its own change, not a side effect of a lock refresh.
#
# Compiled to `requirements-dev.txt` (pinned, hashed). The constraint line keeps
# every package these share with the runtime at the runtime lock's version, so
# installing both locks in one pip command never conflicts.
-c requirements.txt

mypy==2.1.0
types-requests==2.33.0.20260518
types-psutil==7.2.2.20260518
